Assertions:
[ERRORS label=b_create] errors[] empty {SPEC} (VCST-5628)
[DATA label=b_create] data.createReturn.status = Draft {SPEC} (VCST-5628)
[ERRORS label=b_submit] errors[] empty {SPEC} (VCST-5628)
[DATA label=b_submit] data.submitReturn.status = Requested {SPEC} (VCST-5628)
[ERRORS label=get_role] HTTP 200 {OBSERVED}
[DATA label=get_role] body.roles.0.roleId is non-null {OBSERVED}
[ERRORS label=before_revoke] errors[] empty {SPEC} (VCST-5884 AC-1: a holder reads the organization)
[DATA label=before_revoke] data.organizationReturns.items[?number={{B_NO}}].number = {{B_NO}} {SPEC} (VCST-5884 AC-3)
[ERRORS label=state_revoked] HTTP 200 {OBSERVED}
[COUNT label=state_revoked] body.roles.length = 0 {OBSERVED}
[ERRORS label=after_revoke] errors[] non-empty {DOC} (VirtoOZ PlatformUserGuide: organization-scoped roles are applied on the server immediately, only the signed-in session is stale; execution lane B observed the same token refused on the next call)
[DATA label=after_revoke] errors[0].extensions.code = Forbidden {OBSERVED} (kb KB-9E0ED0F4)
[NULL label=after_revoke] data.organizationReturns {DOC} (VirtoOZ PlatformUserGuide, as above)
[ERRORS label=state_regranted] HTTP 200 {OBSERVED}
[DATA label=state_regranted] body.roles.0.roleId = {{VIEW_ROLE_ID}} {OBSERVED}
[ERRORS label=after_regrant] errors[] empty {OBSERVED} (execution lane B: the server re-reads roles on every call, so the OLD token is answered again after the restore; BL-B2B-005 and ECL-4.3 concern what the TOKEN carries, so they are not cited for this server leg)
[DATA label=after_regrant] data.organizationReturns.items[?number={{B_NO}}].number = {{B_NO}} {OBSERVED} (execution lane B, as above)
[ERRORS label=cleanup_b] errors[] empty {SPEC} (VCST-5628)

